# NetworkGraph implementation map

This document describes the currently mounted code. It is not a deployment or model-quality certification.

- `backend/main.py` mounts the NetworkGraph API at `/api/network`.
- `backend/networkgraph/routers/intelligence.py` collects the modular routers under `/intelligence`.
- `GET /api/network/intelligence/graph` builds subreddit, domain, and author views. Modes are `spread`, `sources`, `amplifiers`, and `all`.
- `GET /api/network/intelligence/timeline` returns narrative counts from `subreddit_edges` and totals from `daily_volume`.
- `backend/networkgraph/database.py` opens `analysis_v2.db` read-only. `backend/patch_db.py` populates persistent tables from the bundled CSVs during container startup.
- `backend/networkgraph/routers/utils.py` normalizes narrative identifiers and applies graph filters. Narrative metadata is joined with topic mappings and timestamped graph-edge records.
- `backend/networkgraph/routers/search.py` contains the optional AI node-analysis endpoint; provider calls require configuration and are separate from deterministic graph reads.

The bundled analysis is a historical snapshot. Local tests and a frontend build do not verify external providers, PostgreSQL, concurrent deployments, or production readiness. See the root and backend READMEs for setup, test commands, provenance, health semantics, and known limits.
